+| Prop work: original exact solvers, rewinds, descriptor/row edits, all soft kinds; full simulation across all five cars/biomes | 16,924/16,924 headless and desktop Mobile; earlier focused 1,924/1,924 Compatibility |
+| Existing tyre equivalence | 13,200 exact whole-state comparisons |
+| Existing compiler goldens / native Winter/raster | 8/8 unchanged; 482/482 |
+| New preparation with task-original native library | 8/8 compiler goldens and 482/482 native/scalar checks |
+| Records / driving / checkpoints / tyre-load | 54 / 72 / 266 / 75 checks passed |
+| Breakable props / burning barrel / rewind | 46 / 54 / 61 passed |
+| Cars, including 15 full five-lap recordings/replays / handling / bridge contacts | 105 / 88 / 16 passed |
+| Road cache / editor preparation / App / achievement notification | 70 / 270 / 141 / 291 passed |
+| Graphical race hitch monitor / personal ghosts / Garage exterior inspection | 47 / 38 / 45 passed |
+| Existing wash, persistence and Garage/race lifecycle | 1,383 headless / 1,402 Compatibility passed; captures retained |
+| Pinned import / final script parse | Passed; 942 scripts, zero failures |
+
+Two pre-existing regression failures remain documented, with assertions intact: `test_surface_modes.gd` reports its oil-placement failure (50 checks, one failure) on both task-original and fixed sources; `test_breakable_contract.gd` reports the same 689 historical no-breakable physics assertions out of 2,219 on both. Its old geometry checks and legacy movable-prop comparisons pass. This task does not change those fixtures or assert a globally green suite. The current-version independent physics comparisons above pass exactly.
+
+Initial corrections are retained in the evidence report: a RefCounted destruction-hook ownership approach was replaced with a tree-owned writer; JSON-number normalization and expected-corruption parsing were corrected in the save test; the cancellation test now requests cancellation within the native callback sampling cadence. Two isolated-copy reproduction commands initially lacked historical fixture/report directories and were rerun after fixing only that test environment. An incorrect Garage test filename was rejected before execution. No failing gameplay invariant was removed or relaxed.
